            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="VAR03" sex="2">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Elizabeth</forename>
                        <surname>Varley</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1784">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1864"/>
                    <occupation>Artist</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p> The entry is 'call on Mulready cum Varley' 15.3.1805 and then 13.4.1805 mrs Varley at Thos
                            Hope's.  John Varley DNB 1778-1842 married Esther Gisborne in 1803 (see
                            Gisborne) and his friend and pupil William Mulready DNB 1786-1863
                            married Varley's sister Elizabeth also in 1803 (said to have been an
                            unhappy marriage). Elizabeth was an artist herself). John Varley's brothers
                            Cornelius and John Fleetwood, both in DNB, were as yet unmarried. Thomas
                            Hope DNB 1769-1831 was an "enlightened patron of young and promising
                            artists" </p>
                    </note>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
